At last I had the courage/interest/whatever to finish this game! The
poor knight had suffered enough in the Orcus town where I had left him
because I wanted to start some new games (I love the early game when
everything is still hmm, possible)...

The game went pretty easily. Nothing really interesting happened. I
don't remember the early game because I played it a month ago. I
changed alignment 'cause I don't like playing lawfuls (especially if
the god doesn't give me Grayswandir) and lawful knights are even
worse... I felt kinda stupid entering a leprechaun hall, kicking the
wall to wake them up and then chasing them around the dungeon. Is that
more honourable thing to do?!

Yes, being chaotic was much more pleasing. And today Robbie went
totally crazy. All that time in Orcus town must have caused that... He
wanted to walk on the wild side and so he became an arch-lich. That was
fun. All of a sudden his AC was -52 (and his gear wasn't as brilliant
as it could have been because he was going wishless). The downside was
he couldn't twoweapon anymore. :( He used only Excalibur after that. I
know it sucks but he didn't have anything better. Umm, except
Demonbane... Is that better than Excalibur?

Well, he put on an amulet of unchanging and shouted "To the wizard's
tower!" Wizard went down with a wand of death, no problemo. Sanctum was
tougher than usually because I had only 150 hit points. At some points
I took the amulet of unchanging off so that I don't die YASD.

And finally Robbie got the amulet! And wow, the run up was wonderful as
chaotic! Only twice I got thrown back. This was my first chaotic
ascension and it was much more enjoyable "without" the mysterious
force. I always get totally irritated with neutrals and lawfuls on the
way up. Slashem has it so much better! The one who created the
mysterious force is a complete jerk and probably has never ascended
him/herself.

And just a thought: Don't leave Asmodeus and Baalzebub behind and then
leave the game for two weeks. It was annoying kill them on the way up,
especially Asmodeus who gave me the cold attack and I gave him the same
treatment + some excaliburing...

The planes went smoothly. I didn't have conflict or free action but who
needs those! Astral was tough! Once again I took the unchanging off. I
had only 25 hitpoints left at that point. I teleported everything out
of my way (except Death). I forgot that knights can jump. Doh! But the
first altar was the correct one. Yeehaa! I did it! What a feeling!!! ;D

